// Unsigned less-than, the unsigned reading of `<` that docs/SPEC.md 6 gives
// the flat store.
//
// `id` compares integers signed, and flipping both sign bits turns the
// unsigned order into the signed one: it maps 0 to the most negative word and
// the largest word to the most positive, preserving order everywhere in
// between. So this needs no instruction of its own.

ult(word a, word v) {
  word p = a ^ 0x8000000000000000;
} return word ult_at(p, v ^ 0x8000000000000000);

ult_at(word p, word q) {
  word v = 0;
  if(p < q) {
    v = 1;
  }
} return word v;
